# What Vercel does not need. Kept deliberately SMALL — see the warning below before adding to it.
#
# The Foundry project's own build output and every local test artifact are irrelevant to the
# deployed page. Nothing here is required at runtime: `/api/proof` reads the chain over plain
# JSON-RPC and needs no key, no wallet and no `.env`.
#
# TWO RULES, both learned from a deploy that failed four times in a row:
#
# 1. ANCHOR EVERY PATTERN WITH A LEADING SLASH. These are gitignore semantics, so a bare `lib/`
#    matches a directory named lib at ANY depth — including `node_modules/next/dist/lib/`, which
#    the deployment needs. That produced
#      ENOENT: lstat '/vercel/path0/node_modules/next/dist/lib/constants.js'
#    on the runner. `out/` and `cache/` are the same trap: npm packages contain both names.
#
# 2. DO NOT IGNORE ANYTHING THE PREBUILT OUTPUT REFERENCES. `vercel build` writes a `filePathMap`
#    into each `.vc-config.json` naming the files the function expects at deploy time — ~27k
#    entries here, spanning node_modules, .next, docs, src, lib, data, contracts and scripts.
#    (`docs/`, `contracts/`, `src/` and `data/` are not dead weight: the `/evidence/[...path]`
#    route serves those files at runtime.) Ignoring one is not a smaller upload, it is a broken
#    deploy — `/.next/` here cost an ENOENT on `.next/package.json`.
#
# To check a candidate before adding it:
#   python3 -c "import json,glob;print({k.split('/')[0] for f in glob.glob('.vercel/output/functions/**/.vc-config.json',recursive=True) for k in (json.load(open(f)).get('filePathMap') or {})})"

/out/
/cache/
/broadcast/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/.lighthouseci/
/docs/index41-pitch-deck.pdf
